const char s3295[] = "Required throttle for level flight at minimum airspeed FW_AIRSPD_MIN (sea level, standard atmosphere) Set to 0 to disable mapping of airspeed to trim throttle below FW_AIRSPD_TRIM.";
const char s3296[] = "FW_THR_CRUISE";
const char s3297[] = "Cruise throttle";
const char s3298[] = "This is the throttle setting required to achieve the desired cruise speed. Most airframes have a value of 0.5-0.7.";
const char s3299[] = "FW_THR_IDLE";
const char s3300[] = "Idle throttle";
const char s3301[] = "This is the minimum throttle while on the ground (\"landed\") in auto modes.";
const char s3302[] = "This is the minimum throttle while on the ground For aircraft with internal combustion engines, this parameter should be set above the desired idle rpm. For electric motors, idle should typically be set to zero. Note that in automatic modes, \"landed\" conditions will engage idle throttle.";
const char s3303[] = "This is the minimum throttle while on the ground For aircraft with internal combustion engine this parameter should be set above desired idle rpm.";
const char s3304[] = "FW_THR_LND_MAX";
const char s3305[] = "Throttle limit during landing below throttle limit altitude";
const char s3306[] = "During the flare of the autonomous landing process, this value will be set as throttle limit when the aircraft altitude is below FW_LND_TLALT.";
const char s3307[] = "FW_THR_MAX";
const char s3308[] = "Throttle limit max";
const char s3309[] = "Applies in any altitude controlled flight mode. Should be set accordingly to achieve FW_T_CLMB_MAX.";
const char s3310[] = "Maximum throttle limit in altitude controlled modes. Should be set accordingly to achieve FW_T_CLMB_MAX.";
const char s3311[] = "This is the maximum throttle % that can be used by the controller. For overpowered aircraft, this should be reduced to a value that provides sufficient thrust to climb at the maximum pitch angle PTCH_MAX.";
const char s3312[] = "FW_THR_MIN";
const char s3313[] = "Throttle limit min";
const char s3314[] = "Applies in any altitude controlled flight mode. Usually set to 0 but can be increased to prevent the motor from stopping when descending, which can increase achievable descent rates.";
const char s3315[] = "Minimum throttle limit in altitude controlled modes. Usually set to 0 but can be increased to prevent the motor from stopping when descending, which can increase achievable descent rates. For aircraft with internal combustion engine this parameter should be set for desired idle rpm.";
const char s3316[] = "This is the minimum throttle % that can be used by the controller. For electric aircraft this will normally be set to zero, but can be set to a small non-zero value if a folding prop is fitted to prevent the prop from folding and unfolding repeatedly in-flight or to provide some aerodynamic drag from a turning prop to improve the descent rate. For aircraft with internal combustion engine this parameter should be set for desired idle rpm.";
const char s3317[] = "FW_THR_SLEW_MAX";
const char s3318[] = "Throttle max slew rate";
const char s3319[] = "Maximum slew rate for the commanded throttle";
const char s3320[] = "FW_THR_TRIM";
const char s3321[] = "Trim throttle";
const char s3322[] = "Required throttle (at sea level, standard atmosphere) for level flight at FW_AIRSPD_TRIM";
const char s3323[] = "This is the throttle setting required to achieve FW_AIRSPD_TRIM during level flight.";
const char s3324[] = "FW_TKO_AIRSPD";
const char s3325[] = "Takeoff Airspeed";
const char s3326[] = "The calibrated airspeed setpoint during the takeoff climbout. If set <= 0, FW_AIRSPD_MIN will be set by default.";
const char s3327[] = "The calibrated airspeed setpoint TECS will stabilize to during the takeoff climbout. If set <= 0.0, FW_AIRSPD_MIN will be set by default.";
const char s3328[] = "FW_TKO_PITCH_MIN";
const char s3329[] = "Minimum pitch during takeoff";
const char s3330[] = "FW_T_ALT_TC";
const char s3331[] = "Altitude error time constant";
const char s3332[] = "FW_T_CLMB_MAX";
const char s3333[] = "Maximum climb rate";
const char s3334[] = "This is the maximum calibrated climb rate that the aircraft can achieve with the throttle set to FW_THR_MAX and the airspeed set to the trim value. For electric aircraft make sure this number can be achieved towards the end of flight when the battery voltage has reduced.";
const char s3335[] = "This is the maximum climb rate that the aircraft can achieve with the throttle set to THR_MAX and the airspeed set to the trim value. For electric aircraft make sure this number can be achieved towards the end of flight when the battery voltage has reduced.";
const char s3336[] = "This is the best climb rate that the aircraft can achieve with the throttle set to THR_MAX and the airspeed set to the default value. For electric aircraft make sure this number can be achieved towards the end of flight when the battery voltage has reduced. The setting of this parameter can be checked by commanding a positive altitude change of 100m in loiter, RTL or guided mode. If the throttle required to climb is close to THR_MAX and the aircraft is maintaining airspeed, then this parameter is set correctly. If the airspeed starts to reduce, then the parameter is set to high, and if the throttle demand required to climb and maintain speed is noticeably less than FW_THR_MAX, then either FW_T_CLMB_MAX should be increased or FW_THR_MAX reduced.";
const char s3337[] = "FW_T_CLMB_R_SP";
const char s3338[] = "Default target climbrate";
const char s3339[] = "In auto modes: default climb rate output by controller to achieve altitude setpoints. In manual modes: maximum climb rate setpoint.";
const char s3340[] = "The default rate at which the vehicle will climb in autonomous modes to achieve altitude setpoints. In manual modes this defines the maximum rate at which the altitude setpoint can be increased.";
const char s3341[] = "FW_T_F_ALT_ERR";
const char s3342[] = "Fast descend: minimum altitude error";
const char s3343[] = "Minimum altitude error needed to descend with max airspeed and minimal throttle. A negative value disables fast descend.";
const char s3344[] = "FW_T_HRATE_FF";
const char s3345[] = "Height rate feed forward";
const char s3346[] = "FW_T_I_GAIN_PIT";
const char s3347[] = "Integrator gain pitch";
const char s3348[] = "Increase it to trim out speed and height offsets faster, with the downside of possible overshoots and oscillations.";
const char s3349[] = "Integrator gain on the pitch part of the control loop. Increase it to trim out speed and height offsets faster, with the downside of possible overshoots and oscillations.";
const char s3350[] = "This is the integrator gain on the pitch part of the control loop. Increasing this gain increases the speed at which speed and height offsets are trimmed out, but reduces damping and increases overshoot. Set this value to zero to completely disable all integrator action.";
const char s3351[] = "FW_T_I_GAIN_THR";
const char s3352[] = "Integrator gain throttle";
const char s3353[] = "This is the integrator gain on the throttle part of the control loop. Increasing this gain increases the speed at which speed and height offsets are trimmed out, but reduces damping and increases overshoot. Set this value to zero to completely disable all integrator action.";
const char s3354[] = "FW_T_PTCH_DAMP";
const char s3355[] = "Pitch damping gain";
const char s3356[] = "Pitch damping factor";
const char s3357[] = "This is the damping gain for the pitch demand loop. Increase to add damping to correct for oscillations in height. The default value of 0.0 will work well provided the pitch to servo controller has been tuned properly.";
const char s3358[] = "FW_T_RLL2THR";
const char s3359[] = "Roll -> Throttle feedforward";
const char s3360[] = "Is used to compensate for the additional drag created by turning. Increase this gain if the aircraft initially loses energy in turns and reduce if the aircraft initially gains energy in turns.";
const char s3361[] = "Increasing this gain turn increases the amount of throttle that will be used to compensate for the additional drag created by turning. Ideally this should be set to approximately 10 x the extra sink rate in m/s created by a 45 degree bank turn. Increase this gain if the aircraft initially loses energy in turns and reduce if the aircraft initially gains energy in turns. Efficient high aspect-ratio aircraft (eg powered sailplanes) can use a lower value, whereas inefficient low aspect-ratio models (eg delta wings) can use a higher value.";
const char s3362[] = "FW_T_SEB_R_FF";
const char s3363[] = "Specific total energy balance rate feedforward gain";
const char s3364[] = "FW_T_SINK_MAX";
const char s3365[] = "Maximum descent rate";
const char s3366[] = "This sets the maximum descent rate that the controller will use. If this value is too large, the aircraft can over-speed on descent. This should be set to a value that can be achieved without exceeding the lower pitch angle limit and without over-speeding the aircraft.";
const char s3367[] = "FW_T_SINK_MIN";
const char s3368[] = "Minimum descent rate";
const char s3369[] = "This is the minimum calibrated sink rate of the aircraft with the throttle set to THR_MIN and flown at the same airspeed as used to measure FW_T_CLMB_MAX.";
const char s3370[] = "This is the sink rate of the aircraft with the throttle set to THR_MIN and flown at the same airspeed as used to measure FW_T_CLMB_MAX.";
const char s3371[] = "FW_T_SINK_R_SP";
const char s3372[] = "Default target sinkrate";
const char s3373[] = "In auto modes: default sink rate output by controller to achieve altitude setpoints. In manual modes: maximum sink rate setpoint.";
const char s3374[] = "The default rate at which the vehicle will sink in autonomous modes to achieve altitude setpoints. In manual modes this defines the maximum rate at which the altitude setpoint can be decreased.";
const char s3375[] = "FW_T_SPDWEIGHT";
const char s3376[] = "Speed <--> Altitude weight";
const char s3377[] = "Adjusts the amount of weighting that the pitch control applies to speed vs height errors. 0 -> control height only 2 -> control speed only (gliders)";
const char s3378[] = "Speed <--> Altitude priority";
const char s3379[] = "This parameter adjusts the amount of weighting that the pitch control applies to speed vs height errors. Setting it to 0.0 will cause the pitch control to control height and ignore speed errors. This will normally improve height accuracy but give larger airspeed errors. Setting it to 2.0 will cause the pitch control loop to control speed and ignore height errors. This will normally reduce airspeed errors, but give larger height errors. The default value of 1.0 allows the pitch control to simultaneously control height and speed. Set to 2 for gliders.";
const char s3380[] = "This parameter adjusts the amount of weighting that the pitch control applies to speed vs height errors. Setting it to 0.0 will cause the pitch control to control height and ignore speed errors. This will normally improve height accuracy but give larger airspeed errors. Setting it to 2.0 will cause the pitch control loop to control speed and ignore height errors. This will normally reduce airspeed errors, but give larger height errors. The default value of 1.0 allows the pitch control to simultaneously control height and speed. Note to Glider Pilots - set this parameter to 2.0 (The glider will adjust its pitch angle to maintain airspeed, ignoring changes in height).";
const char s3381[] = "FW_T_SPD_DEV_STD";
const char s3382[] = "Airspeed rate measurement standard deviation";
const char s3383[] = "For the airspeed filter in TECS.";
const char s3384[] = "Airspeed rate measurement standard deviation for airspeed filter";
const char s3385[] = "This is the measurement standard deviation for the airspeed rate used in the airspeed filter in TECS.";
const char s3386[] = "FW_T_SPD_OMEGA";
const char s3387[] = "Complementary filter \"omega\" parameter for speed";
const char s3388[] = "This is the cross-over frequency (in radians/second) of the complementary filter used to fuse longitudinal acceleration and airspeed to obtain an improved airspeed estimate. Increasing this frequency weights the solution more towards use of the airspeed sensor, whilst reducing it weights the solution more towards use of the accelerometer data.";
const char s3389[] = "FW_T_SPD_PRC_STD";
const char s3390[] = "Process noise standard deviation for the airspeed rate";
const char s3391[] = "This is defining the noise in the airspeed rate for the constant airspeed rate model of the TECS airspeed filter.";
const char s3392[] = "Process noise standard deviation for the airspeed rate in the airspeed filter";
const char s3393[] = "This is the process noise standard deviation in the airspeed filter filter defining the noise in the airspeed rate for the constant airspeed rate model. This is used to define how much the airspeed and the airspeed rate are filtered. The smaller the value the more the measurements are smoothed with the drawback for delays.";
const char s3394[] = "FW_T_SPD_STD";
const char s3395[] = "Airspeed measurement standard deviation";
const char s3396[] = "Airspeed measurement standard deviation for airspeed filter";
const char s3397[] = "This is the measurement standard deviation for the airspeed used in the airspeed filter in TECS.";
const char s3398[] = "FW_T_STE_R_TC";
const char s3399[] = "Specific total energy rate first order filter time constant";
const char s3400[] = "This filter is applied to the specific total energy rate used for throttle damping.";
const char s3401[] = "FW_T_TAS_R_TC";
const char s3402[] = "True airspeed rate first order filter time constant";
const char s3403[] = "This filter is applied to the true airspeed rate.";
