const char s6721[] = "RD_MAX_THR_YAW_R";
const char s6722[] = "Yaw rate turning left/right wheels at max speed in opposite directions";
const char s6723[] = "Rover Differential \342\200\213";
const char s6724[] = "This parameter is used to calculate the feedforward term of the closed loop yaw rate control. The controller first calculates the required speed difference between the left and right motor to achieve the desired yaw rate. This desired speed difference is then linearly mapped to normalized motor commands. A good starting point is half the speed the rover drives at maximum throttle (RD_MAX_THR_SPD)). Increase this parameter if the rover turns faster than the setpoint, and decrease if the rover turns slower.";
const char s6725[] = "RD_MISS_SPD_GAIN";
const char s6726[] = "Tuning parameter for the speed reduction during waypoint transition";
const char s6727[] = "The waypoint transition speed is calculated as: Transition_speed = Maximum_speed * (1 - normalized_transition_angle * RM_MISS_VEL_GAIN) The normalized transition angle is the angle between the line segment from prev-curr WP and curr-next WP interpolated from [0, 180] -> [0, 1]. Higher value -> More speed reduction during waypoint transitions. Set to -1 to disable any speed reduction during waypoint transition.";
const char s6728[] = "RD_TRANS_DRV_TRN";
const char s6729[] = "Yaw error threshhold to switch from driving to spot turning";
const char s6730[] = "This threshold is used for the state machine to switch from driving to turning based on the error between the desired and actual yaw. It is also used as the threshold whether the rover should come to a smooth stop at the next waypoint. This slow down effect is active if the angle between the line segments from prevWP-currWP and currWP-nextWP is smaller then 180 - RD_TRANS_DRV_TRN.";
const char s6731[] = "RD_TRANS_TRN_DRV";
const char s6732[] = "Yaw error threshhold to switch from spot turning to driving";
const char s6733[] = "This threshold is used for the state machine to switch from turning to driving based on the error between the desired and actual yaw.";
const char s6734[] = "RD_WHEEL_TRACK";
const char s6735[] = "Wheel track";
const char s6736[] = "Distance from the center of the right wheel to the center of the left wheel.";
const char s6737[] = "RD_YAW_STK_GAIN";
const char s6738[] = "Yaw stick gain for Manual mode";
const char s6739[] = "Assign value <1.0 to decrease stick response for yaw control.";
