const char s9583[] = "Module Param - The module's control mechanism";
const char s9584[] = "PWM Mode: Commands a fraction of battery voltage. This changes as the battery voltage changes. This is the least safe mode because the upper throttle limit is determined by the battery voltage. Voltage Mode: Commands a voltage. The motor will behave the same way throughout the life of a battery, assuming the commanded voltage is less than the battery voltage. You must set the MAX_VOLTS parameter. Velocity Mode: Closed-loop, commands a velocity. The controller will adjust the applied voltage so that the motor spins at the commanded velocity. This mode has faster reaction times. Only use this if you know the properties of your propeller. You must set the MAX_VELOCITY parameter.";
